{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 13513 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2044d8f832ff1ace53e9eded6d4a6d50a13b79d7d4bbf1fc7f684ee0bb212f94" :edb/db-before-t 13512 :edb/db-after-t 13513 :edb/tx-data [[13194139546825 50 #inst "2026-11-09T00:08:50.278Z" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1117 #edb/ref 17592186755528 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1117 #edb/ref 17592186755542 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186048885 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186049072 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186049589 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186050373 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186050850 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755439 1075 #edb/ref 17592186755466 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755439 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755439 1077 "answer" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755439 1078 #edb/ref 17592186755466 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755439 1079 #uuid "01f863d5-254e-57f2-a85a-2914586a0a07" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755440 1062 #uuid "074e478a-0bc7-5924-a0e6-5a17dd7f26cc" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755440 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755548 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755441 1080 "e^y-x^3" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755441 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755441 1083 #uuid "0921f7be-2261-5c5e-82af-e49dea670fa2" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755442 1080 "The guaranteed set is $\\{(x_0,y_0)\\in\\mathbb R^2:y_0\\ne0\\}$. The function $f(x,y)=(xy)^{3/5}$ is continuous everywhere, while $f_y=\\frac35x^{3/5}y^{-2/5}$ is continuous on $y\\ne0$.\n\nIf $y_0\\ne0$, choose a small open rectangle that avoids $y=0$. Both continuity hypotheses then hold. If $y_0=0$, every open rectangle contains points $(x,0)$ with $x\\ne0$, where $f_y$ does not exist, so the theorem does not guarantee uniqueness. The value $f_y(0,0)=0$ alone does not give continuity on a rectangle." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755442 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755442 1083 #uuid "10599fd1-7f2b-52d4-b3af-3f587c18857c" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755443 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755508 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755443 1071 "**(b)** Verify that $y=1/(c-x)$, where $c$ is a constant, is a solution of $y'=y^2$." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755443 1072 #uuid "118f3004-9f6d-5030-b2e1-7feb9d0dfce7" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755443 1074 "Differentiate with respect to $x$ while holding $c$ fixed. Both sides equal $1/(c-x)^2$. The singular value $x=c$ must be excluded." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755444 1062 #uuid "15d2c5c3-0b9e-500d-a9b9-1376be7f4837" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755444 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755537 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755458 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755498 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755517 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755523 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755530 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755532 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1071 "**(b)** Which curves are solution curves? Select all that apply." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1072 #uuid "192392f6-44d7-504d-83c7-de78dbcd98d1" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755445 1074 "The indicated solution curves are $C,D,E$. They follow the field and pass the vertical line test on their regular graph portions. Curves $A$ and $B$ follow the field geometrically but fold back and do not represent single-valued functions of $x$; $F$ is not tangent to the field.\n\nThe differential equation is undefined on $y=0$ and $y=4/3$. A classical solution is considered only on an open interval where the selected graph avoids those lines; the apparent meeting point at the origin is excluded." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755446 1080 "false" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755446 1081 "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755446 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755446 1083 #uuid "1ae9a436-e49f-5915-8698-8c65adbed4d2" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755447 1075 #edb/ref 17592186755560 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755447 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755447 1077 "answer" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755447 1078 #edb/ref 17592186755560 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755447 1079 #uuid "1b0be3d4-1da9-5424-9263-75fe204b9cbf" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755448 1058 #edb/ref 17592186755440 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755448 1062 #uuid "1ce9a959-4bb1-588b-8a60-0512539c646b" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755448 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755497 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755449 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755492 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755449 1071 "**(a)** Find every $(x_0,y_0)$ for which Theorem 2.3.1 guarantees at least one local solution. Identify $f$ and $f_y$ and their continuity sets as directed above." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755449 1072 #uuid "1da7a288-d9ee-5194-a63e-449903272ed0" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755449 1074 "The odd denominator in the exponent allows negative arguments: $(xy)^{3/5}$ is real and continuous everywhere. Do not discard the axes for existence. Part (a) uses condition (a) of the theorem, not the stronger derivative condition for uniqueness." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755450 1084 #edb/ref 17592186755444 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755450 1084 #edb/ref 17592186755476 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755450 1084 #edb/ref 17592186755553 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755450 1085 "Source question: Problem 1(a–c), printed/PDF page 2; page 3 is spare workspace.\n\nConsider $y'=3e^{-y}x^2$. Hint: $\\ln(1)=0$." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755450 1086 #uuid "1f38f1bb-9bc4-55c9-b2b7-0f18fd90c546" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755450 1087 #edb/ref 17592186755553 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755451 1080 "e^{-x}" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755451 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755451 1083 #uuid "2135cc87-45da-5b27-b628-6f189d4e6687" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755452 1080 "false" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755452 1081 "The complete curve folds back in x and fails the vertical line test." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755452 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755452 1083 #uuid "23393cfc-4870-5b87-b5d8-cd06d38152e0" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755453 1064 "**MTH 256 — E1 (source title: Quiz 1)**\n\nDue: 2026-10-06\nExam date: 2026-10-06\nDate source: user-provided exam date; no submission time supplied\nDate imported: 2026-11-08\nSource: [256-E-1.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FE-1%2F256-E-1.pdf)\n\nThe complete scan preserves the student’s handwritten work. Quiz answers, worked explanations, and branch/domain corrections in this note are independently authored study additions, not an instructor key.\n\n## Instructions\n\nThe original assessment contains four problems worth 40 points and allows 40 minutes. Wait for the TA to begin and start the timer. Only a writing implement and eraser are permitted; calculators are not allowed. Complete all four problems. Problem 1 requires no supporting work. Problem 4 allows the stated variation-of-parameters alternative.\n\nStudy-link coverage is partial for distinguishing geometric integral curves from solution graphs. The vertical-line-test supporting link is outside the normal route (Test Preparation)." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755453 1066 #uuid "272e59af-eaaf-5eb6-bcdc-320e64043c53" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755453 1067 "Assignment information" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755454 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755524 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755454 1071 "Source question: Problem 3, printed/PDF page 6.\n\nFind all implicit solutions of\n\n$$y'=\\frac{12x^3+9x^2+1}{10y^4+6y^2+2y+3}.$$\n\nWrite the implicit relation as {{answer}} $=C$." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755454 1072 #uuid "2b670c8d-3950-51c3-91b1-4d760b76f12a" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755454 1074 "Separate and integrate:\n\n$$\\int(10y^4+6y^2+2y+3)\\,dy=\\int(12x^3+9x^2+1)\\,dx,$$\n\nso $2y^5+2y^3+y^2+3y=3x^4+3x^3+x+C$. Differentiating recovers the ODE. Its denominator is positive for all real $y$, since\n\n$$10y^4+6y^2+2y+3=10y^4+6(y+1/6)^2+17/6>0.$$\n\nThus no denominator-zero values must be removed from this implicit family." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755455 1058 #edb/ref 17592186755448 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755455 1062 #uuid "2bf51323-8e98-59fa-9fd2-292ed7419cab" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755455 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755546 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755456 1080 "false" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755456 1081 "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755456 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755456 1083 #uuid "2c35ffba-6d7c-5e41-890b-bb9828a7254e" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755481 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755487 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755504 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755505 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755507 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755563 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1071 "**(a)** Which curves are integral curves? Select all that apply." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1072 #uuid "30bcd75d-100a-5db4-a865-cbd5ed1332a6" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755457 1074 "In the source's geometric convention, $A,B,C,D,E$ are integral curves: their tangents follow the field. Curve $F$ does not.\n\nSeparating variables gives $(4y-3y^2)\\,dy=2x\\,dx$, so regular integral-curve pieces lie on levels of $2y^2-y^3-x^2=C$. Differentiating this relation recovers the ODE wherever $y\\ne0,4/3$. The displayed folds and loop are allowed for geometric integral curves; they need not each be one graph $y(x)$." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755458 1075 #edb/ref 17592186755456 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755458 1075 #edb/ref 17592186755539 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755458 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755458 1077 "E" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755458 1078 #edb/ref 17592186755539 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755458 1079 #uuid "3272277a-c801-5feb-8eb6-5a73417e96ad" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755459 1080 "true" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755459 1081 "This is a graph, but it is not tangent to the field." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755459 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755459 1083 #uuid "36d089ac-c271-537d-99f8-7c6719688313" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755460 1058 #edb/ref 17592186755529 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755460 1062 #uuid "3748993b-e0ad-54dc-a0be-2a8cc3c68fcf" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755460 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755533 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755461 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755439 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755461 1071 "**(b)** Find all solutions to the equation." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755461 1072 #uuid "37a94c9f-3744-5f95-b630-578a0901ab14" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755461 1074 "Solving $y^2=x^4+C$ gives both signs. Require strict positivity, because equality would give $y=0$ and make the original equation undefined. A continuous nonzero solution cannot change sign inside its interval. Differentiate either branch to check $y'=2x^3/y$." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755462 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755495 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755462 1071 "Source question: Problem 3, PDF page 4 (10 points).\n\nSolve the initial value problem $y'=2\\cos x$, $y(0)=3$.\n\n$y=$ {{answer}}." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755462 1072 #uuid "383e4acd-ffca-5f9b-8bb1-faed1d3422fa" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755462 1074 "Integration gives $y=2\\sin x+C$. At $x=0$, $3=C$, so $y=2\\sin x+3$ on $\\mathbb R$. Its derivative is $2\\cos x$ and its value at zero is $3$." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755463 1080 "true" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755463 1081 "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755463 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755463 1083 #uuid "395f90c7-2326-5b80-ba7e-c82cd6c2eb76" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755464 1080 "false" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755464 1081 "The curve follows the field directions, including its turning portions." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755464 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755464 1083 #uuid "3d948d6c-7597-548c-9165-2289d229e024" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755465 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048697 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755465 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049481 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755465 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049589 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755465 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050905 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755465 1089 #edb/ref 17592186755450 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755465 1090 #uuid "3e2313be-95f7-5c86-96e0-3cea7910d450" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755466 1080 "All real solutions are restrictions of\n\n$$y(x)=\\varepsilon\\sqrt{x^4+C},\\qquad \\varepsilon\\in\\{-1,1\\},$$\n\nwith fixed $C\\in\\mathbb R$ and fixed sign on a connected interval where $x^4+C>0$. The maximal intervals are:\n\n- $C>0$: $\\mathbb R$;\n- $C=0$: $(-\\infty,0)$ or $(0,\\infty)$;\n- $C<0$: $(-\\infty,-(-C)^{1/4})$ or $((-C)^{1/4},\\infty)$.\n\nThere is no $y=0$ solution because the equation is undefined there." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755466 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755466 1083 #uuid "3ec64d09-d570-5e6d-b0b5-91824799cbb9" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755467 1075 #edb/ref 17592186755555 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755467 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755467 1077 "answer" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755467 1078 #edb/ref 17592186755555 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755467 1079 #uuid "3ef6107d-c187-588d-8ec7-9a629826351c" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755468 1080 "true" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755468 1081 "This curve is locally a graph y(x), tangent to the field where the ODE is defined." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755468 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755468 1083 #uuid "41d1f5f5-1d3b-529a-bea6-cb90618ba1d0" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755469 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755467 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755469 1071 "**(c)** Solve $y'=y^2$, $y(1)=1$.\n\n$y=$ {{answer}}." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755469 1072 #uuid "42ac2f6d-24a8-5b15-bb5a-4eceb4f450ad" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755469 1074 "The family in part (b) gives $1=1/(c-1)$, so $c=2$ and $y=1/(2-x)$. Its maximal interval containing $x=1$ is $(-\\infty,2)$. Check that $y'=1/(2-x)^2=y^2$ and $y(1)=1$. The equilibrium $y=0$ does not satisfy this initial condition." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755470 1058 #edb/ref 17592186755474 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755470 1062 #uuid "42e77825-1e67-54ed-801a-af2a58c2b0fe" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755470 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755457 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755471 1084 #edb/ref 17592186755473 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755471 1084 #edb/ref 17592186755514 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755471 1084 #edb/ref 17592186755518 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755471 1085 "Source question: Problem 4(a–c), printed/PDF page 7; page 8 is spare workspace.\n\nConsider $y'=2x^3/y$." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755471 1086 #uuid "44602230-c040-565f-b6c8-7b09b005f172" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755471 1087 #edb/ref 17592186755514 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755472 1075 #edb/ref 17592186755547 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755472 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755472 1077 "answer" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755472 1078 #edb/ref 17592186755547 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755472 1079 #uuid "448c417f-6b60-54c1-94fa-be922863df2a" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755473 1058 #edb/ref 17592186755518 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755473 1062 #uuid "49005526-4228-5a7d-ae9e-f70d0a154e66" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755473 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755461 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755474 1062 #uuid "495802aa-ac7a-5671-9f73-ab3c379d0342" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755474 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755445 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755475 1080 "2\\sin x+3" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755475 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755475 1083 #uuid "4b37d26c-93bd-51d6-bbe3-a71409fedd93" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755476 1058 #edb/ref 17592186755444 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755476 1062 #uuid "4f5ccaed-c81c-5c65-850f-5c3ec941e76e" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755476 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755521 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755477 1058 #edb/ref 17592186755543 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755477 1062 #uuid "52809ac6-abf1-588b-af6b-9efddd06a206" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755477 1063 #edb/ref 17592186755479 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755478 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755484 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755478 1071 "**(a)** Compute an integrating factor for $y'-y=e^x$.\n\n$I(x)=$ {{answer}}." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755478 1072 #uuid "54cf4014-0850-58a9-9d8b-2ad541d9c8ba" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755478 1074 "The standard form is $y'+P(x)y=Q(x)$ with $P(x)=-1$. Thus $I(x)=e^{\\int-1\\,dx}=e^{-x}$. Any nonzero constant multiple works; the normal