 1078 #edb/ref 17592186755502 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755499 1079 #uuid "84404310-f19f-511a-ad6f-2e5ca2e0427c" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755500 1068 #edb/ref 17592186755472 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755500 1071 "**(a)** Verify that $y=1/(5-x)$ is a solution of $y'=y^2$." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755500 1072 #uuid "860969f5-95ee-5009-8088-3d650a5746b8" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755500 1074 "Differentiate the proposed function and compare with the square of the function. The chain rule contributes two minus signs: $\\frac{d}{dx}(5-x)^{-1}=-(5-x)^{-2}(-1)$. Merely integrating or rewriting the function does not verify the equation." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755501 1080 "true" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755501 1081 "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755501 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755501 1083 #uuid "8e631e52-140f-5743-9bc1-18651d6e288c" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755502 1080 "For any $C\\in\\mathbb R$,\n\n$$y(x)=\\ln(x^3+C),\\qquad x\\in(-\\sqrt[3]{C},\\infty).$$\n\nThese are the maximal real solution intervals; restrictions to smaller open intervals are also solutions." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755502 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755502 1083 #uuid "90711706-247e-5cfc-8a84-f190bef4b691" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755503 1080 "false" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755503 1081 "The curve follows the field directions on its regular portions." 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755503 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755503 1083 #uuid "926f22f2-cf3d-5200-aa7c-c5a017e4e048" 13194139546825 17592186502323 true] [17592186755504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186755503 131